{"name":"Cottage Rose","hex":"#d9a89a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cottage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small house.","A seasonal home of any size or stature, a recreational home or a home in a remote location."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stay at a seasonal home, to go cottaging.","To have homosexual sex in a public lavatory; to practice cottaging."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cottage"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cottage","blocks":[{"text":"A cottage during England's feudal period was the holding by a cottager of a small house with enough garden to feed a family and in return for the cottage, the cottager had to provide some form of service to the manorial lord. However, in time cottage just became the general term for a small house. In modern usage, a cottage is usually a modest, often cosy dwelling, typically in a rural or semi-rural location and not necessarily in England. The cottage orné, often quite large and grand residences built by the nobility, dates back to a movement of \"rustic\" stylised cottages of the late 18th and early 19th century during the Romantic movement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Country_cottage%2C_Inch_Island_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3951065_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Country_cottage%2C_Inch_Island_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3951065_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottage"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/South_Devon_cottage_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81799.jpg/500px-South_Devon_cottage_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81799.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/South_Devon_cottage_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81799.jpg/500px-South_Devon_cottage_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81799.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A typical cottage in Devon, with walls built of cob and a thatched roof","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouth_Devon_cottage_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81799.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Miners_Cottages%2C_Pit_Village%2C_Beamish_Museum%2C_5_September_2013.jpg/500px-Miners_Cottages%2C_Pit_Village%2C_Beamish_Museum%2C_5_September_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"h